      "benchmark": {
        "hands": {
          "zh": "论文 v2 列五种本体：Franka 两指平行夹爪、xArm7 连杆夹爪或 Panda 夹爪、Kinova Gen3＋Panda 夹爪、双 Franka 平行夹爪、G1 双三指手。真机 VLA 为 Franka＋Robotiq 2F-85；当前项目页宣称支持 17 种本体，不等于论文五种配置之外均已完成同等评测。",
          "en": "Paper v2 lists five embodiments: Franka with a two-finger parallel gripper, xArm7 with a linkage or Panda gripper, Kinova Gen3 with a Panda gripper, bimanual Franka with parallel grippers, and G1 with two three-finger hands. Hardware VLA uses Franka with Robotiq 2F-85. The current project advertises 17 embodiments; this does not establish equivalent paper evaluation of all later additions."
        },
        "tasks": {
          "zh": "28 项任务：装配 9、收纳 4、益智 6、形变物／液体 4、切割 2、移动操作 3；单次物理执行可达约半小时。Agent 需提交 solve(env) 程序，主比较每任务给 4 小时开发预算，按独立隐藏评分及成功率、耗时、成本评测；不是 28×全部本体的完整组合。",
          "en": "Twenty-eight tasks cover assembly (9), packing (4), puzzles (6), deformables/liquids (4), cutting (2) and loco-manipulation (3), with physical execution horizons up to about 30 minutes. Agents submit solve(env) programs under a four-hour development budget per task in the main comparison, evaluated through independent hidden grading, success, time and cost. The benchmark is not a full 28-task-by-all-embodiment evaluation matrix."
        },
        "cross_hand": {
          "zh": "六项任务把已验证的 Franka 程序作为提示，迁移到 Kinova Gen3 和 xArm7；三者共用 Panda 夹爪，主要验证跨机械臂代码适配，不是跨手型策略共享。G1 等其他末端有任务支持，但未报告同一策略在所有手型上的配对零样本验证。",
          "en": "On six tasks, verified Franka programs serve as hints for Kinova Gen3 and xArm7. All three carry the Panda gripper, testing cross-arm program adaptation rather than cross-hand policy sharing. Other effectors such as G1 hands have task support, but matched zero-shot shared-policy validation across all hand morphologies is not reported."
        },
        "release": {
          "zh": "官方 GitHub 已公开基准、Agent 评测、EmbodiedSWE-Gen 与 VLA 训练／评测代码，Hugging Face 已公开任务和场景仿真资产；支持基于 Isaac Lab 的运行，形变物套件使用 Newton。完整生成示范集及训练好的 VLA／Agent checkpoint 下载尚未核实；资产包不等于示范数据集。",
          "en": "Official GitHub releases the benchmark, agent evaluation, EmbodiedSWE-Gen and VLA training/evaluation code; Hugging Face provides task and scene simulation assets. Execution is based on Isaac Lab, with Newton for the deformable suite. Downloads of complete generated demonstration datasets and trained VLA/agent checkpoints remain unverified; the asset collection is not a demonstration dataset."
        },
        "highlight": {
          "zh": "EmbodiedSWE 构建包含 28 项长时序机器人操作任务的仿真基准，评测 Coding Agent 编程求解及跨任务、跨本体迁移能力，并将成功程序扩增为示范数据训练 VLA；以独立评分和回放检查连接“程序求解评测→可验证训练数据”。",
          "en": "EmbodiedSWE benchmarks coding-agent program synthesis and cross-task/cross-embodiment transfer on 28 long-horizon simulated robotics tasks, then expands successful programs into VLA demonstrations, linking program-solving evaluation to verified training data through independent grading and replay checks."
        }
      },
      "evaluation_scope": {
        "zh": "求解 Agent 可读取完整仿真状态并调试程序，使用通用 IK／操作空间等控制器；独立评分环境禁用物体状态写入，不能把特权状态求解成绩当作纯视觉策略成绩。Gen 从成功解扩增场景、策略、中间阶段、动力学和视觉，筛选成功且可回放的轨迹。仿真 SmolVLA 实验限六项子任务，输入多视角 RGB、指令及 8 维关节／夹爪状态，输出关节目标；部分任务放宽了原始基准成功条件，不能与完整 28 项 Agent 成绩直接比较。真机用 500 条仿真示范微调 π₀.₅-DROID 拆台灯，无真机示范参与微调；十次试验最终旋出并取下灯泡为 20%，checkpoint 按真机表现选择。另有合成 400 个环境对 Coding Agent 做 PPO 后训练，未完成未见任务评测；该 RL 不等于主线 VLA 动作策略训练。",
        "en": "Solver agents inspect full simulator state and debug programs using generic IK/operational-space controllers; independent graders disable object-state writes. Privileged-state solver results are not vision-only policy results. Gen diversifies scenes, strategies, intermediate phases, dynamics and appearance, retaining successful replay-verified trajectories. Simulated SmolVLA experiments cover only six tasks, taking multi-view RGB, instructions and 8-D joint/gripper state to joint targets. Some success criteria are relaxed relative to the original benchmark, precluding direct comparison with full 28-task agent results. Hardware lamp disassembly finetunes π₀.₅-DROID on 500 simulation demonstrations without real demonstrations for finetuning; final bulb unscrewing/extraction succeeds in 20% of ten trials, with checkpoint selection based on hardware performance. A separate study PPO-post-trains a coding agent on 400 generated environments without completed held-out evaluation; this RL is not the main VLA action-learning procedure."
      },
